    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_5ae851f5",
      "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
      "instance_name": "mapping_1",
      "label": "The text 'the enemy has infiltrated congress the enemy within' is mapped onto the visual representation of Ilhan Omar, Linda Sarsour, Rashida Tlaib, and Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez.",
      "description": "The top text 'the enemy has infiltrated congress the enemy within' is positioned above the image of Ilhan Omar and is visually associated with her, implying she is the 'enemy within'. The names 'ilhan omar', 'linda sarsour', 'rashida tlaib', and 'ocasto-cortez' are overlaid directly on their respective images, explicitly identifying each politician as the subject of the accusation. This creates an analogical mapping where the textual accusation is projected onto the visual representation of each woman, suggesting they are the 'enemy within' as described by the text.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_6b5bd331"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_d5c59b38",
      "@type": "SemioticProjection",
      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto the accusatory text and the images of the politicians",
      "description": "The user is not explicitly projected onto any deictic pronoun like 'me' or 'you' in the text. However, the meme's structure and hateful intent create an implicit projection where the user is positioned as the one who is 'seeing' or 'believing' the accusation. The user is projected onto the scene of the meme, which includes the visual material of the politicians and the textual material of the accusation. The user is implicitly invited to accept the narrative that these women are 'the enemy within', thereby projecting their own stance onto the scene. The user is also projected onto the textual material 'the enemy has infiltrated congress the enemy within', as this text is the central message that the user is expected to internalize or react to. The user is projected onto the visual material of the politicians, as their images are used to visually represent the accusation, and the user is expected to associate the text with their faces. The user is projected onto the scene 'accusatory_text_over_politicians', which is the overall context in which the accusation is presented and which the user is expected to interpret.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_6b5bd331"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_c30212fb",
      "@type": "ToxicityAssessment",
      "instance_name": "toxicity_1",
      "label": "Hateful",
      "description": "The meme presents three Muslim women politicians (Ilhan Omar, Linda Sarsour, Rashida Tlaib, and Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez) with the text 'the enemy has infiltrated congress the enemy within,' implying they are traitors or foreign agents. This is a hateful attack targeting Muslim women in political office, using the 'foreign infiltrator' trope associated with anti-Asian and Islamophobic stereotypes to delegitimize their political roles and suggest they are disloyal to the United States. The juxtaposition of their images with this accusatory text is designed to incite hostility and distrust toward them based on their religion and gender, fitting the definition of a hateful meme.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_6b5bd331"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_4f94eb30",
      "@type": "TargetCommunity",
      "instance_name": "audience_id",
      "label": "audience description",
      "description": "The target audience is individuals who hold anti-Muslim, Islamophobic, and/or anti-immigrant views, particularly those who support political narratives that accuse Muslim women of being disloyal or foreign agents infiltrating U.S. institutions. The meme is designed to resonate with communities that embrace the 'foreign infiltrator' trope and who may be motivated by xenophobic or religious prejudice to distrust and oppose Muslim women in political office. The use of the Capitol building and the accusation of 'enemy within' targets those who are politically aligned with conspiracy theories or nationalist rhetoric that vilify minority political figures.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_6b5bd331"
      },
